# CRITICAL RULES - ALWAYS FOLLOW

## 1. Environment Variables
- ❌ NEVER hardcode localhost URLs in source code
- ✅ ALWAYS use environment variables: import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL
- ✅ ALWAYS provide fallbacks that use VITE_APP_URL first, then localhost
- ⚠️ CRITICAL: Backend APP_URL must be https://naqashthaheem.com (affects all storage URLs)
- ⚠️ CRITICAL: Frontend VITE_API_URL must be https://naqashthaheem.com/api

## 2. Database Migrations
- ❌ NEVER run direct SQL commands (ALTER TABLE, etc.)
- ✅ ALWAYS create proper migration files
- ✅ ALWAYS include Schema::hasColumn() checks
- ✅ ALWAYS include Schema::hasTable() checks
- ✅ ALWAYS make migrations idempotent (safe to run multiple times)
- ✅ ALWAYS test migrations locally before deploying

## 3. Storage & File URLs
- ❌ NEVER construct storage URLs manually with hardcoded domains
- ✅ ALWAYS use Storage::disk('public')->url() in backend
- ✅ ALWAYS use API-provided image_url in frontend
- ✅ ALWAYS ensure APP_URL is correct (storage URLs depend on it)
- ⚠️ CRITICAL: Storage symlinks must exist in BOTH locations:
  - public_html/api/public/storage
  - public_html/storage

## 4. Frontend Build
- ❌ NEVER deploy frontend without checking for localhost URLs
- ✅ ALWAYS verify: grep -r "localhost" dist/ before deploying
- ✅ ALWAYS use .env.production for production builds
- ✅ ALWAYS set VITE_APP_URL in addition to VITE_API_URL
- ✅ ALWAYS clear browser cache after deployment

## 5. API Development
- ❌ NEVER use Auth::check() in controllers when middleware already checks
- ✅ ALWAYS rely on middleware for authentication
- ✅ ALWAYS validate required fields in API requests
- ✅ ALWAYS test with both JWT tokens AND API tokens
- ✅ ALWAYS check nullable constraints before inserting data

## 6. File Uploads
- ❌ NEVER upload files directly to workflow/course endpoints
- ✅ ALWAYS use two-step process:
  1. Upload to /api/files (get file_id)
  2. Attach file_id to resource
- ✅ ALWAYS check file_id field name (underscore, not space)

## 7. Cache Management
- ⚠️ CRITICAL: After changing APP_URL, ALWAYS run:
  - php artisan config:clear
  - php artisan config:cache
  - Restart PHP-FPM
- ✅ ALWAYS clear caches after deployment
- ✅ ALWAYS rebuild config cache in production

## 8. GitHub Actions
- ❌ NEVER use heredoc (<<) syntax in YAML scripts
- ✅ ALWAYS use echo statements for multi-line content
- ✅ ALWAYS export environment variables before building
- ✅ ALWAYS verify secrets are set in GitHub repository

## 9. Testing Before Production
- ❌ NEVER push directly to production without local testing
- ✅ ALWAYS test locally first (localhost:8001 backend, localhost:3000 frontend)
- ✅ ALWAYS test all CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)
- ✅ ALWAYS test file uploads
- ✅ ALWAYS test with API tokens (not just JWT)
- ✅ ALWAYS verify storage URLs in API responses
- ✅ ALWAYS check database schema matches code expectations
- ✅ ALWAYS run migrations locally before deploying
- ✅ ALWAYS check for console errors in browser
- ✅ ALWAYS verify API responses with Postman/curl

## 10. Production Deployment Checklist
- [ ] All migrations have safety checks
- [ ] No localhost URLs in code
- [ ] Frontend .env has production URLs
- [ ] Backend APP_URL set correctly
- [ ] Storage symlinks created
- [ ] Permissions set (775 for storage)
- [ ] Caches cleared and rebuilt
- [ ] Browser cache cleared after deployment

# Common Mistakes & Solutions

## Mistake 1: Images showing localhost URLs
**Cause:** APP_URL not set or config cache not cleared
**Solution:** 
```bash
# Backend
sed -i 's|APP_URL=.*|APP_URL=https://naqashthaheem.com|' backend/.env
php artisan config:clear && php artisan config:cache

# Frontend  
echo "VITE_API_URL=https://naqashthaheem.com/api" > frontend/.env
npm run build
```

## Mistake 2: Storage files return 404
**Cause:** Missing symlinks
**Solution:**
```bash
cd public_html/api/public
ln -sf ../../../backend/storage/app/public storage
cd ../../
ln -sf ../backend/storage/app/public storage
```

## Mistake 3: Migration fails with "column already exists"
**Cause:** Missing Schema::hasColumn() check
**Solution:** Always wrap column additions:
```php
if (!Schema::hasColumn('table', 'column')) {
    $table->string('column');
}
```

## Mistake 4: 422 Unprocessable Content on file attach
**Cause:** Sending wrong field names or wrong data format
**Solution:** Check API expects file_id (underscore), not "file id"

## Mistake 5: Frontend build has localhost URLs
**Cause:** Built with wrong .env or hardcoded URLs
**Solution:**
- Remove ALL hardcoded localhost URLs
- Use environment variables everywhere
- Verify build: grep -r "localhost" dist/

## Mistake 6: API keys not showing (500 error)
**Cause:** Model tries to decrypt fields during JSON serialization, fails and crashes
**Solution:**
```php
// Always hide encrypted fields from JSON
protected $hidden = ['api_key'];

// Always handle decryption errors gracefully
protected function apiKey(): Attribute {
    return Attribute::make(
        get: function ($value) {
            try {
                return decrypt($value);
            } catch (\Exception $e) {
                \Log::warning("Decryption failed: " . $e->getMessage());
                return null;
            }
        }
    );
}
```

## Mistake 7: OAuth redirecting to localhost in production
**Cause:** Hardcoded localhost URLs in OAuth callback
**Solution:**
```php
// ❌ WRONG
return redirect('http://localhost:3000/auth/success?token=' . $token);

// ✅ CORRECT
$frontendUrl = config('app.frontend_url', config('app.url'));
return redirect($frontendUrl . '/auth/success?token=' . $token);

// In config/app.php add:
'frontend_url' => env('FRONTEND_URL', env('APP_URL')),

// In .env set:
FRONTEND_URL=https://naqashthaheem.com
```

-Always make changes and keep it prepare for production